 changes through the food model, and label unverified safety as unverified rather than silently assigning zero added hazard. Report actual decay changes, elapsed time, input/output amounts, water change when measurable, and any evidenced nutritional or safety changes. A controlled comparison uses both actual trajectories, with differences in location and handling disclosed; it does not fabricate a hypothetical control observation.\\\\nLifecycle and maintenance: persist batch IDs, placement, progress, consumed effort, observations and last update tick. Interruption of active work retains completed placement and physical state; resume revalidates the same batch and charges only remaining work. Any passive exposed batch continues normal environmental processing while the actor does something else. Inspection and optional turning require actual actor action; weather response and protection are not automatic. Stop ends managed exposure, not ordinary spoilage, and returns or leaves the surviving batch according to actual ownership, reach and placement. Cancellation releases unconsumed reservations exactly once; elapsed time, spent energy, lost water, spoilage, destructive samples and consumed materials are never refunded. Death stops the actor's work and releases project locks under existing death/ownership rules, without teleporting food or undoing exposure; physical food continues to deteriorate. Development/review waiting advances neither world time nor processing. The product is a traceable exposed-food batch with recorded outcomes, and only becomes labeled successfully preserved when the implemented criteria have actually been met.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No pleasure or satisfaction is awarded for requesting, registration, learning, starting a timer, inspection clicks or a success label. If the existing experience engine supports it, a genuinely informative measured outcome, including failed drying or faster spoilage, may qualify for verified information gain only when measurements support a personally applicable new conclusion. Deduplicate equivalent observations and overlapping probe/trial claims by actor, batch, tested relation and evidence interval. This development proposes no new reward grant, account, budget, goal or permission change; use only already authorized bounded experience rules with their existing caps, cooldowns and decay. Repeated legitimate hands-on maintenance may count only under existing modest practice rules, not as unlimited novelty. Do not grant physical comfort from food placement; the comfort ceiling remains 10. Eating continues to supply basic nutrition independently of mood.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable, reusable events for actual placement, inspection, turning, environmental damage, removal, interruption and verified outcome, each carrying actor when applicable, exact batch and location references, mode, tick, progress state and publicly observable changes. Provide reusable food-batch visual metadata: component, resource appearance, placement/support, intact or altered form, exposed/in-progress/interrupted/removed/spoiled state, and visible surface changes only when supported. Keep analytical decay readings and uncertainty in the inspection report rather than pretending that a precise hidden value is visible. Do not show slices, smoke, racks, dryness, safety badges or preserved-food completion art without the corresponding real process and evidence. An incomplete, unsupported or failed trial must remain visibly pending, unverified or failed, never display preservation success. Observation events alone do not authorize experience rewards.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

